{
  "id": "competitive-enzyme-moieties-second-biology",
  "name": "Competitive enzyme inhibition with explicit binding and moiety budgets",
  "description": "Substrate and inhibitor compete for the same free enzyme. Six species retain inhibitor sequestration and all three conserved moieties, beyond the active uninhibited Michaelis-Menten example; no quasi-steady-state approximation. Illustrative five rates(2,0.5,0.4,5,0.1), initial substrate2,enzyme0.1,inhibitor0.4,complexes/product0. Horizon100 and RK4step0.02 are our choices. Signed net-rate flows encode the stated differential equations. No clamps or resets. These educational equations are not fitted biological forecasts.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1080/25765299.2020.1844369",
  "reference": "Mathematical modeling for enzyme inhibitors with slow and fast subsystems (2020), Competitive inhibition, Eqs10-11.",
